 - **Model tools** (`plans/api.md` "Model tools"):
   - **Character sheet has 7 images**, shown as two groups: face close-ups (Face · front, Face · ¾, Face · profile) and full body (front, ¾, side, back). The face ¾ slot is optional, like a missing face close-up.
   - **Enhance** (profile → Character sheet → Enhance): realism Off / Subtle / Balanced / Strong and upscale Off / 2× / 4× (either can be off, not both), the total estimate before you start ("6 images · about $0.26"), then review each image with a before/after slider: Keep, Reject or Retry one. Kept images replace their slots; the old sheet is saved as a previous version (**Versions**, restorable; restoring saves the current sheet first).
-  - **Outfit face close-ups** (2026-11-11; Dress up was removed): every outfit has 7 pictures, its four angles and three face close-ups with its own hair, make-up and face accessories (made from her base faces and the outfit front). Hover a picture to Redo it; an older outfit offers "Add face close-ups". Shots with an outfit send only its pictures.
+  - **Outfit face close-ups** (2026-11-11; Dress up was removed): every outfit has 7 pictures, its four angles and three face close-ups with its own hair, make-up and face accessories (made from her base faces and the outfit front). Hover a picture to Redo it; right-click "Move to…" or drag it onto another slot to fix a picture in the wrong place (they swap); an older outfit offers "Add face close-ups". Shots with an outfit send only its pictures.
   - **Image models** (owner only, Settings → Engines): the model for every image step (New shots, Edits, Enhance · realism / upscale) with its price line and compatibility. **Change** opens a searchable catalog served by the server (Replicate collections or search; name, owner, description, runs, price line, compatible?), or paste owner/model; the advanced view shows how MUSE fills the model's inputs and lets the owner set extra inputs (never the safety checker). **Default** goes back to the contract's model. A small owner-only **Model** chooser on Shoot, Enhance and Dress up overrides it for one run (`models` in the request); members never see it.
   - **Archive** (owner, profile ⋯ → Archive model): she disappears from every list and picker; **Settings → Archived models** restores her. New work on an archived model reads "This model is archived · restore her in Settings → Archived models".
   - `ModelToolsTests` cover decoding every new shape, the any-model estimates (per unit, by time, unknown), labels and price lines, request encoding, and the demo flows (Enhance review → apply → restore, Dress up Both → whole-set pick → new outfit, discard and failure releasing the hold, archive, owner-only checks).
